# Cloudflare Pages reads this file to customize response headers.
# These are self-contained, single-file HTML pages (fonts/images/scripts
# all base64-embedded inline), so a full page load is a few hundred KB
# to ~800KB and briefly shows a loading placeholder while it downloads
# and decodes. Cloudflare's default `Cache-Control: max-age=0,
# must-revalidate` forces a network round trip on every single visit,
# even when nothing changed, making that loading flash happen far more
# often than necessary.
#
# max-age=60 treats the page as fresh for a minute (no network check at
# all), and stale-while-revalidate=86400 means that for up to a day
# after that, the browser shows the cached copy instantly while quietly
# re-fetching a fresh one in the background for next time. New pushes
# still show up within a minute or so; repeat visits in between load
# instantly instead of re-downloading.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=86400
